WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.485
Watch recursive calls build up and return their results.

00:00:04.485 --> 00:00:07.692
Calls progress through 3, 2, 1 and 0.

00:00:07.692 --> 00:00:10.900
Zero stops recursion; the waiting calls then finish.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.305
What makes a recursive function stop safely?

00:00:14.305 --> 00:00:19.115
The base case ends the calls; the recursive step must move closer to it.
